  "pli-tv-bu-vb-ss8:1.4.35": "<i lang='pi' translate='no'>Idaṁ saṅghassa katikasaṇṭhānaṁ, imaṁ kālaṁ pavisitabbaṁ, imaṁ kālaṁ nikkhamitabbanti</i> might be read as “These are the Sangha’s agreements, this is the time to enter, this is the time to leave,” thereby excluding the word “concerning”. In other words, although I have rendered it as such, it is not clear that there is a connection between them. <a href='https://suttacentral.net/pli-tv-kd18/en/brahmali#1.2.22'>Kd 18:1.2.22</a>, however, makes it clear that the first phrase is to be read in conjunction with the following two. ",
  "pli-tv-bu-vb-ss8:1.4.36": "",
  "pli-tv-bu-vb-ss8:1.5.1": "<i lang='pi' translate='no'>Mettiyabhūmajakā bhikkhū</i> can be read either as referring to two monks, Mettiya and Bhūmajaka, or as a group of monks led by these two. I have not been able to find any clear evidence that it refers to a group, and so I prefer the more straightforward reading that it only refers to the two monks. ",
